            <h2>Train Duration, Distance, and Travel Time Overview</h2>
            <p>Traveling from Washington to Boston covers roughly 393-394 miles (632-634 km) along the Northeast Corridor, linking the nation's capital with New England's cultural and economic hub. This is one of Amtrak's premier routes, with the Acela Express offering America's fastest train service and the Northeast Regional providing a more economical alternative.</p>

